    "narrative": "The standout play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21), who benefits from a prime matchup against the 4.40 xERA of Sandy Alcantara. His score is bolstered by a +14% dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable wind-out forecast, positioning him as our most reliable engine for runs and RBI. **Trevor Story** (66.33) also ranks among our strongest starts; while the 4.57 xERA of Brandon Young is manageable, the 16% park factor boost and 14% SP skill advantage outweigh the inherent risk of his #8 spot in the lineup. Despite the scarcity of stolen bases, we are banking on **Trevor Story** to exploit his underlying potential here, even with the projected 60% chance of an elite hold from the opposing bullpen.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (45.13), who sits just outside the active threshold. While **Travis Bazzana** carries a solid platoon edge against J. Soriano, his efficiency is currently lower than the floor established by **Griffin Conine** (58.94) and **Josh Naylor** (58.71), both of whom are projected for higher volume and better situational deployment in their respective lineups. We are also monitoring **Dalton Rushing** (41.12), whose score remains marginal due to an unfavorable L/L matchup against Quinn Mathews; should his official lineup spot drop lower than the anticipated #9, he will be on thin ice to preserve our remaining game caps.\n\nBeyond the daily roster, we continue to stash high-ceiling assets like **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood**, both of whom are unavailable today due to schedule gaps. While we navigate the day with starters like **Brice Turang** (60.04) and **Isaac Paredes** (65.84), we must remain disciplined with our depth\u2014including **Max Muncy**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and bench pieces like **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Gabriel Moreno**, and **Zach McKinstry**.